  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "resnetlab-stmt-1",
      "quote": "To train a neural network, we use **Backpropagation**.",
      "block_id": "resnetlab-block-2",
      "section": "The Vanishing Gradient Problem",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "resnetlab-stmt-2",
      "quote": "This algorithm calculates how much each weight contributed to the final error (loss) so we can adjust the weights to reduce that error.",
      "block_id": "resnetlab-block-2",
      "section": "The Vanishing Gradient Problem",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "resnetlab-stmt-3",
      "quote": "During backpropagation, to find the gradient of the loss $\\mathcal{L}$ with respect to the first layer's weights, we must multiply the derivatives of *every* layer in the network:",
      "block_id": "resnetlab-block-3",
      "section": "The Vanishing Gradient Problem",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "resnetlab-stmt-4",
      "quote": "This was first mathematically accurately described by \\citeauthor{hochreiter1991vanishing} in his \\cite[Diplomarbeit]{hochreiter1991vanishing}, while the term 'Vanishing Gradient' was first coined by Yoshua Bengio et al. in their \\citeyear{bengio1994learning} paper '\\citetitle{bengio1994learning}'.",
      "block_id": "resnetlab-block-4",
      "section": "The Vanishing Gradient Problem",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "resnetlab-stmt-5",
      "quote": "**Downsampling:** Reducing Height/Width (Stride > 1).",
      "block_id": "resnetlab-block-8",
      "section": "Handling Dimension Mismatches ($1 \\times 1$ Convs)",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "resnetlab-stmt-6",
      "quote": "**Channel Expansion:** Increasing the number of filters (Depth).",
      "block_id": "resnetlab-block-9",
      "section": "Handling Dimension Mismatches ($1 \\times 1$ Convs)",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "resnetlab-stmt-7",
      "quote": "Interactive lab The Gradient Highway An error signal of size 1 starts at the loss and is sent back through every layer.",
      "block_id": "resnetlab-block-10",
      "section": "Handling Dimension Mismatches ($1 \\times 1$ Convs)",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "resnetlab-stmt-8",
      "quote": "A plain layer multiplies it by its local derivative; a residual block multiplies it by 1 + ∂F/∂x.",
      "block_id": "resnetlab-block-10",
      "section": "Handling Dimension Mismatches ($1 \\times 1$ Convs)",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "resnetlab-stmt-9",
      "quote": "Make the network deeper and see who still hears the signal.",
      "block_id": "resnetlab-block-10",
      "section": "Handling Dimension Mismatches ($1 \\times 1$ Convs)",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "resnetlab-stmt-10",
      "quote": "plain network: ∏ a l residual network: ∏ (1 + b l ) node brightness = gradient size at that layer",
      "block_id": "resnetlab-block-11",
      "section": "Handling Dimension Mismatches ($1 \\times 1$ Convs)",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "resnetlab-stmt-11",
      "quote": "Local derivative per plain layer 0.90",
      "block_id": "resnetlab-block-13",
      "section": "Handling Dimension Mismatches ($1 \\times 1$ Convs)",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "resnetlab-stmt-12",
      "quote": "🎲 New random initialization",
      "block_id": "resnetlab-block-14",
      "section": "Handling Dimension Mismatches ($1 \\times 1$ Convs)",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "resnetlab-stmt-13",
      "quote": "Plain: gradient at layer 1 – Residual: gradient at layer 1 – Residual / plain –",
      "block_id": "resnetlab-block-15",
      "section": "Handling Dimension Mismatches ($1 \\times 1$ Convs)",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "resnetlab-stmt-14",
      "quote": "Identity shortcut — shapes match",
      "block_id": "resnetlab-block-16",
      "section": "Handling Dimension Mismatches ($1 \\times 1$ Convs)",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "resnetlab-stmt-15",
      "quote": "Input x [64, 64, 3] Conv path F(x) [64, 64, 3] Output F(x) + x [64, 64, 3]",
      "block_id": "resnetlab-block-17",
      "section": "Handling Dimension Mismatches ($1 \\times 1$ Convs)",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "resnetlab-stmt-16",
      "quote": "Projection shortcut — 4 → 2 channels",
      "block_id": "resnetlab-block-18",
      "section": "Handling Dimension Mismatches ($1 \\times 1$ Convs)",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "resnetlab-stmt-17",
      "quote": "Source x [H, W, 4] 1×1 conv W s [1, 1, 4, 2] Projected W s x [H, W, 2]",
      "block_id": "resnetlab-block-19",
      "section": "Handling Dimension Mismatches ($1 \\times 1$ Convs)",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "resnetlab-stmt-18",
      "quote": "y = F(x, {W i }) + W s x — the 1×1 kernel mixes channels at each pixel without looking at its neighbours.",
      "block_id": "resnetlab-block-20",
      "section": "Handling Dimension Mismatches ($1 \\times 1$ Convs)",
      "kind": "statement"
    }
  ],
